<title>UK: Reuters 6th ex-UK/Americas air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 6th ex-UK/Americas air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK air cargo rates to the United States and Latin America per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		   April 25	     April 11</p>
<p>		 UNITED STATES</p>
<p> LON-CHI	   0.76		   0.74</p>
<p> LON-JFK	   0.65		   0.62</p>
<p> LON-LAX	   0.80		   0.77</p>
<p> LON-MIA	   0.65		   0.63</p>
<p> LON-HOU	   0.84		   N.A.</p>
<p>		 LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> LON-SAO	   1.90		   1.86</p>
<p> LON-BUE	   2.05		   2.00</p>
<p> LON-SCL	   1.92		   1.84</p>
<p> LON-CCS	   1.30		   1.30</p>
<p> LON-BOG	   1.40		   N.A.</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax 5017</p>
